{
  "registered": "2026-11-24",
  "about": "The shadow lab (2026-11-24, the operator's approval): pre-registered experiments graded on real results, with no entries needed. Every kept lineup of a saved bank (entered or not) gets its real finish percentile in each of the slate's graded contests; an experiment's treatment lineups are compared to its control lineups from the SAME slate and contest (paired). Written by scripts/dk_eval.py lab (run by ideas, nightly); the definitions below are fixed before the first counted slate and only 'results' is rewritten.",
  "method": {
    "unit": "a slate (draft group) with a saved bank, a record and at least one graded contest of LAB_MIN_ENTRIES (100) entries or more; a slate on or after the experiment's registration date counts toward its planned nights, earlier slates are a look-back only",
    "lineups": "the bank's kept lineups (final), entered or not; a lineup drawn under several tags counts for each of them (the ideas grade's shared-lineup credit)",
    "finish_percentile": "100 x (contest entries - real entries scoring more than the lineup) / contest entries: the share of the real field the lineup beats or ties, on the night's real points (the standings' FPTS, else the record's)",
    "top10": "the lineup's place (1 + real entries scoring more) within the contest's top 10% (ceil(0.1 x entries))",
    "paired_difference": "per contest: mean finish percentile of the treatment lineups minus that of the control lineups; per slate: the equal-weight mean over its contests (the primary metric). Top-10% rates are reported the same way, as a secondary",
    "noise": "SE of the nightly paired differences: their sample standard deviation / sqrt(nights)",
    "pass_bar": "after the planned nights: treatment ahead (slate difference > 0) on at least 7 of the 10 AND the pooled difference (the mean of the 10 slate differences) above 2 x noise. Verdict on the first 10 counted slates; later slates are shown but do not change it",
    "ahead": "slate paired difference > 0"
  },
